 2. 🗳️ Trump: Sen. Sullivan should get other Sullivan&#x27;s votes 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios. Photo: Bill Clark/CQ-Roll Call via Getty Images President Trump said today that Alaska Sen. Dan Sullivan (R) should get the votes for Dan J. Sullivan, a candidate in Alaska's tumultuous Senate race with the same name as the incumbent, Axios' Avery Lotz reports .

 🤳 Trump wrote on Truth Social : "The vote totals for the Fake Dan Sullivan, plus the other 'slug' that the Dems put on the Ballot, should be immediately given to the REAL Dan Sullivan, and the Election is over."

 He added: "He easily wins. There is no other fair solution!" Democrat Mary Peltola leads but Sen. Sullivan is close behind, with 78% of the vote counted.

 The challenger Sullivan, who was listed on the ballot as "Sullivan, Daniel J. Jr.," is in last place with 3,600 votes. 📊 In Alaska's ranked-choice system, if no candidate gets more than half of voters' first-place votes, the last-place finisher is eliminated and their ballots are reallocated to voters' next choices until a candidate has a majority.

